<article class="env-definition" id="0CLK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CLK">Definition <span data-tag="0CLK">101.39.10</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. We say $f$ satisfies the <em>existence part of the valuative criterion</em> if for every diagram (<a href="/tag/0CLB" data-tag="0CLB">101.39.1.1</a>) and $\gamma $ as in Definition <a href="/tag/0CLA" data-tag="0CLA">101.39.1</a> there exists an extension $K'/K$ of fields, a valuation ring $A' \subset K'$ dominating $A$ such that the category of dotted arrows for the outer rectangle of the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K') \ar[r] \ar@/^2em/[rr]_{x'} \ar[d]_{j'} &  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K) \ar[d]_ j \ar[r]_-x &  \mathcal{X} \ar[d]^ f \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A') \ar[r] \ar@/_2em/[rr]^{y'} &  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) \ar[r]^-y &  \mathcal{Y} }  \]
</div>
  <p> with induced $2$-arrow $\gamma ' : y' \circ j' \to f \circ x'$ is nonempty. </p>
</article>